{
  "name": "rotunda",
  "version": 1,
  "introduced_by": "saurischia",
  "notes": "The domed hall of Cascadelle: a pale-stone drum 28 m across with 20 columns round it, four arched entrances 7 m across and 11 m clear on the compass points (front is -Z), an open floor inside with a dark-stone long-neck on a plinth in the middle, its head toward the front door, and a shell dome with a glazed lantern, 31 m to the finial. It carves its interior.",
